# Cloudflare's asset layer serves static files (robots.txt, sitemap.xml,
# sw.js, manifest, icons, JS) without ever passing through the Worker's
# middleware — so the headers below are the ONLY way to reach those
# responses. HTML routes go through the Worker (src/middleware.ts sets
# X-Robots-Tag there); this file is the belt-and-braces for everything
# else, and the authoritative source for /sw.js's cache lifetime.
#
# NO WILDCARD ROBOTS RULE HERE: a `/*  X-Robots-Tag: noindex` would ship
# to production too (same asset layer) and noindex every page the
# sitemap advertises. App routes are noindexed by the middleware
# (src/middleware.ts), which only runs on HTML — exactly the split we
# want. Preview-only noindex would need an env-scoped _headers, which
# the deploy pipeline doesn't have; the preview domains are
# unlisted-and-fine (no private data renders signed-out).

# The service worker must revalidate on every load — a cached sw.js
# would pin users to an old worker for up to 24h (the browser default).
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: max-age=0, must-revalidate
